A series of close-up and extreme close-up b-roll shots, detail-focused:

— macro of hands with sticks: stick snapping down on the snare, water exploding upward in spray, droplets sparkling in the sun;

— close-up of a cymbal hit: tip touching the edge, water fanning out, cymbal trembling and glinting;

— low angle on the bass drum: foot on the pedal, beater striking, water shivering on the head;

— close-up of Naomi's face in full drive, water droplets on her skin and glasses, focused gaze;

— hi-hat detail: cymbals closing, a burst of water spray and a spark of light;

— a stick run across the toms top-to-bottom (drum fill), water splashing on each hit, motion blur;

— wider medium shot: the whole kit throwing water spray, sun shining on the drums, Naomi behind it, wind sweeping her hair and the field.
High-speed capture of the splashes (slow-motion accents), camera dynamic, handheld, light shake, fast accents on the beat. <<<audio_1>>>

Photoreal 8K IMAX, large-format 65mm film look, organic grain, cold foggy diffused light, shallow depth of field, heavy haze. Cinematic in-camera realism, restrained Hollywood naturalism. Real-time 24fps, NO slow-motion. Diegetic dialogue + SFX only, NO music, no text, no watermark. ONE continuous take, no cuts, no match-cuts.

CINEMATIC FRAMING: PHASE 1 opens tight and low on <<<0c794756-60c5-4b6c-8a3b-582e2e95ba29>>> in 3/4 chiaroscuro — cool instrument glow one side, soft shadow the other, canopy reflections in her eyes, shallow 65mm DoF, subtle Dutch tilt, face off-centre. On the last "WAIT" the camera makes a bold continuous move — craning/whipping OUT and DOWN to GROUND LEVEL outside at the mecha's feet, catching the sole pneumatics punch the first step and the mecha exploding forward in forced perspective, rim-lit against the foggy sky, debris to lens. One unbroken move from intimate cockpit close-up to low exterior ground-cam. No lingering inside the cabin during the dash.

MULTISHOT — one continuous motion in two flowing phases (no cuts):
PHASE 1 — THE GLANCE & SNAP: tight low 3/4 chiaroscuro on <<<0c794756-60c5-4b6c-8a3b-582e2e95ba29>>> in her cockpit (per <<<848c6674-ef97-48f7-9b75-edcbd3df61d1>>>), glancing around for her team and snapping "WAIT, WAIT, WAIT" — fast and clipped, the three words rattled off RIGHT after one another with NO dramatic pauses, rising in irritation, annoyed at falling behind.
PHASE 2 — THE DASH: on the last "WAIT" she slams the controls; camera cranes out to GROUND LEVEL at the feet as <<<ccc9d249-9056-4ef3-a9a8-d4a64b60227a>>>'s SOLE PNEUMATICS punch the FIRST STEP and it explodes into a heavy hyper-dash straight FORWARD toward the bridge. Snap → instant dash, one continuous move.

FACE / EYES / EMOTION in PHASE 1 (living — IRRITATED about being LATE, NOT terror):
- TONE: impatience/irritation of running late and annoyed about it — like missing a bus and being ticked off. Concerned + irritated + flustered. NOT mortal fear, NOT panic, NOT crying.
- EYES: alive, GLANCING AROUND for the team, impatient narrowing/widening, wet shine.
- BLINKING (mandatory): natural irregular blinking, quick impatient blinks.
- FOREHEAD / FRONTALIS (mandatory): eyebrows drawing together into an IRRITATED knot, brief furrow between the brows, light annoyance creases shifting — exasperation at being late/behind.
- MOUTH/JAW: snapping each "WAIT" fast, clipped, jaw tight, lips pressing between words; quick breath.
- OVERALL: irritated, impatient, hurried, glancing; micro-expressions never still, eyes never dead; grounded annoyance, NOT extreme fear.

SECONDARY_MOTION = ENABLED {
  hair:        (P1) <<<0c794756-60c5-4b6c-8a3b-582e2e95ba29>>>'s hair alive — strands shifting as she snaps the words and turns to glance, flyaways in the cockpit air catching rim light, a lock across her face;
  face:        (P1) blinking (irregular), frontalis/forehead working (irritation knot + furrow), brows together, annoyance creases, eyes glancing/narrowing, lips snapping "WAIT", jaw tension;
  body:        turning/leaning to glance, quick impatient shifts, hands on the sticks, then slamming them into the dash;
  cockpit:     (P1) <<<848c6674-ef97-48f7-9b75-edcbd3df61d1>>> alive — readouts flickering and reflecting in glass and eyes, cool light on her face, dust motes, harness shifting;
  pneumatics:  (P2) sharp burst of vented air/vapour and dust blasting from the sole AT the first step, piston punching the ground hard as that foot drives off the mark;
  atmosphere:  (P2) fog and dust torn back by the dash, wind ripping past, particulate in the wake catching cold backlight;
  debris:      (P2) ground debris and grit cratered up and flung backward and toward the low lens by the pneumatic first step and footfalls;
  ground:      (P2) surface cracking/cratering under the pneumatic first step and heavy footfalls;
  breath:      quick impatient breaths;
  rule:        camera-independent — all continues regardless of camera movement.
